# vocab/queries/vocabulary-role.rq
#
# D1 — the vocabulary-role derivation (spec §2.1, §4.3, §4.4).
#
# NEUROSYMBOLIC GATE (CLAUDE.md §8) — AXIOM, DERIVATION FORM, OPEN WORLD. The rule is
# POSITIONAL and EVIDENCE-POSITIVE throughout: a term is emitted because a triple SHOWS it
# occupying a vocabulary role, never because something is absent. There is no NOT EXISTS, no
# COUNT, no threshold and no tolerance in this file; the closed-world question — "and is it
# declared?" — belongs to the membrane (vocab/shapes/query-declaration-shapes.ttl), which is
# where it is asked.
#
# THE RULE. An owned IRI occupies a vocabulary role in a graph if either
#   (a) it appears in the PREDICATE position of any triple; or
#   (b) it appears in the OBJECT position of a triple whose predicate is one of the sixteen
#       RDFS/OWL/SHACL predicates listed below; or
#   (c) it is reached from an sh:path by following a SHACL property-path expression
#       (spec §4.4) — a term inside a property path IS being used as a property. The
#       construct set is exhaustively fixed by the SHACL recommendation, so clause (c) is
#       complete BY CONSTRUCTION rather than by tuning. Measured yield over the tree:
#       exactly docgov:cites and docgov:citesExternal, which is also the check that it
#       does not over-reach.
#
# The sixteen predicates are STANDARD VOCABULARY — they are the rule itself, not a list of
# owned terms under test. No owned term is ever typed in this file (G3), and no local name is
# ever string-tested. VALUES is used deliberately: SHACL forbids VALUES inside an sh:sparql
# constraint (MEASURED 2026-08-28, R135 F3), but this is a standalone CONSTRUCT and that
# restriction does not apply — confirmed by running it.
#
# GRAPH ?artifact, not a flat union: role is a PER-GRAPH property (spec §2.1) and provenance
# to the file must survive into the membrane's failure message (CLAUDE.md §6).
#
# © 2026 François Rosselet · CC-BY-4.0
PREFIX rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#>
PREFIX etkl: <https://w3id.org/iladub/etkl#>

CONSTRUCT {
    ?artifact a etkl:VocabularyArtifact ;
              etkl:namesTerm ?term .
}
WHERE {
    GRAPH ?artifact {
        {
            # (a) predicate position
            ?s ?term ?o .
        }
        UNION
        {
            # (b) object of a schema predicate
            VALUES ?schemaPredicate {
                rdf:type rdfs:subClassOf rdfs:subPropertyOf rdfs:domain rdfs:range
                owl:equivalentClass owl:equivalentProperty owl:onProperty
                owl:someValuesFrom owl:allValuesFrom
                sh:targetClass sh:path sh:targetSubjectsOf sh:targetObjectsOf
                sh:class sh:datatype
            }
            ?s ?schemaPredicate ?term .
        }
        UNION
        {
            # (c) inside a SHACL property-path expression reachable from sh:path
            ?s sh:path ?pathRoot .
            ?pathRoot ( sh:alternativePath | sh:inversePath | sh:zeroOrMorePath
                      | sh:oneOrMorePath | sh:zeroOrOnePath | rdf:first | rdf:rest )+ ?term .
        }
    }
    FILTER ( isIRI(?term) )
    FILTER ( STRSTARTS(STR(?term), "https://w3id.org/iladub") )
}
